schema:distribution

Definition
..........
A downloadable form of this dataset, at a specific location, in a specific format. This property can be repeated if different variations are available. There is no expectation that different downloadable distributions must contain exactly equivalent information (see also [DCAT](https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-3/#Class:Distribution) on this point). Different distributions might include or exclude different subsets of the entire dataset, for example.

Scope
.....
Domain: Dataset (https://schema.org/Dataset).
Range: DataDownload (https://schema.org/DataDownload).


CDIF
----

Definition
..........
specifies how to download the data in a specific format or access via a web API. This property describes where to get the data and in what format by using the schema:DataDownload type. If user must access data through a landing page, provide link to landing page in the 'url' property for the dataset

Scope
.....
schema:distribution - distributions of the dataset. The AbstractDistribution supertype admits schema:DataDownload (file-based) or schema:WebAPI (service endpoint).
</body>
